# omx-modgui-sync lists the LV2 plugins with lilv; Debian bookworm has no python3-lilv (trixie and later do), so it is a suggestion
Suggests: python3-lilv
Description: panels for LV2 and CLAP plugins, generated from what each plugin declares
 omx-panel makes panels for LV2 and CLAP plugins from what each plugin
 declares. It lays a panel out from a plugin's descriptor (sections, controls,
 roles, the pages of eight a controller shows), writes a MOD GUI for MOD and
 Zynthian in the omx look, imports a plugin's own MOD GUI into a skin package,
 and carries the skin package schema, its validator and the directory skin
 packages are installed into. The omx-panel command runs each; the tools are
 under /usr/share/omx-panel for a build that calls them.
 .
 Its documentation is on openmixer.org.

Package: libomx-panel-render0
Section: libs
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, omx-panel (= ${source:Version})
Description: omx-panel renderer, a library that draws a panel into a pixel buffer
 libomx-panel-render.so.0 draws a panel description in the omx look into a CPU
 pixel buffer and answers input with the one gesture vocabulary. A surface
 loads it at run time (Zynthian's panel view); its look, geometry and fonts
 are omx-panel's.

Package: libomx-panel-render-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: libomx-panel-render0 (= ${binary:Version}), libcjson-dev, ${misc:Depends}
Description: omx-panel renderer, development files
 The header omx_panel_render.h, the libomx-panel-render.so link and the
 omx-panel-render pkg-config file, to build against the omx-panel renderer.
